                    <occupation>Printer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope comments: Perhaps the 1794
                            Grant Alexander Grant was dismissed from his function as an honorary
                            member of the SCI representing the LCS because he refused to give up
                            manuscript of the bill of Carter the bill-sticker (Trials for Treason and
                            Sedition). Alexander Grant printer Wardour St Soho 1794 list of
                            witnesses in treason trials. Bankrupt 1.8.1795, died May 1801 (Maxted).
                            Identified as the Grant at Palmer's.</p><p>Another possibility is: James Grant LL D Rector of St Leonards Shoreditch
                            (Literary Memoirs of Living Authors p 222) supposed to have been
                            concerned in conducting the English Review. Published sermon 1774 vicar
                            of Kempston Beds, Lecturer of St Leonards Shoreditch. </p>
                    </note>
